   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9 · Human-in-the-loop, through the real API\n",
    "\n",
    "Compliance decisions are human-owned. This exercises the actual FastAPI app in\n",
    "memory (`TestClient`): **log in** (JWT), **analyze** a case asynchronously, then an\n",
    "analyst **corrects a field and approves** — and that correction is captured as\n",
    "feedback (the flywheel that later feeds extraction, calibration, and RAG)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "3a9b8718",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-19T20:16:50.875476Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-19T20:16:50.875291Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-19T20:16:53.796341Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-19T20:16:53.795474Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "logged in as role: analyst\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "job: done | case: needs_review | confidence: 0.897\n",
      "after review → reviewed\n",
      "feedback captured: [{'case_id': 'case_00002', 'field': 'expiry', 'corrected_value': '01/01/2030', 'label_kind': 'extraction'}]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n",
    "from evident.api.main import app\n",
    "client = TestClient(app)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1) authenticate (demo creds; RBAC: analyst vs admin)\n",
    "tok = client.post(\"/auth/login\", params={\"username\": \"analyst\", \"password\": \"analyst123\"}).json()\n",
    "headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {tok['access_token']}\"}\n",
    "print(\"logged in as role:\", tok[\"role\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2) analyze asynchronously, then poll the job\n",
    "job = client.post(f\"/cases/{EXP}/analyze\").json()\n",
    "status = client.get(job[\"poll\"]).json()[\"status\"]\n",
    "summary = client.get(f\"/cases/{EXP}\").json()\n",
    "print(\"job:\", status, \"| case:\", summary[\"status\"], \"| confidence:\", summary[\"confidence\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3) analyst reviews: correct a field + approve  (needs the analyst role)\n",
    "review = client.post(f\"/cases/{EXP}/review\",\n",
    "                     params=None,\n",
    "                     json={\"action\": \"request_correction\",\n",
    "                           \"edited_fields\": {\"expiry\": \"01/01/2030\"},\n",
    "                           \"reason\": \"customer supplied a renewed document\"},\n",
    "                     headers=headers).json()\n",
    "print(\"after review →\", review[\"status\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4) the correction is now captured as feedback (admin-only view)\n",
    "admin = client.post(\"/auth/login\", params={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"admin123\"}).json()\n",
    "fb = client.get(\"/feedback\", headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {admin['access_token']}\"}).json()\n",
    "print(\"feedback captured:\", fb[\"feedback\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22df0c18",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note the RBAC in action: `/review` requires the analyst role and `/feedback`\n",
    "requires admin — an unauthenticated call gets 401, the wrong role gets 403. Every\n",
    "action is tied to an identity, which is what makes the audit trail meaningful."
   ]
  },
  {
