   "source": [
    "## 10 · Calibrated confidence\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Confidence\" is defined as **P(a human analyst confirms the automated decision)** and\n",
    "**calibrated** — trained on features with a logistic-regression calibrator, then\n",
    "checked with **Expected Calibration Error** and a reliability diagram (blueprint §10).\n",
    "A perfectly calibrated model sits on the diagonal. Trained with\n",
    "`scripts/train_confidence.py`; here we plot the saved report."
   ]
  },
